Z||000000||Alex2004||04-12-2001||06:35 PM||||i had my interior door panels off today and i was just messing around and i noticed a wire coming off the drivers door latch from the inside, they are black and grey, and it has a little plug but is not plugged up to anything.  But the passenger door doesn't have this, and there is also a "warning, protected by alarm" stick on my back window like it used to have an alarm cause it doesn't now.  But just wondering what it is.  Thanks!<P>               Alex...||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-12-2001||07:14 PM||||If it is connected to your latch on the inside, that is the door ajar switch connector.  The passenger one should also have this.  Look again for missing wires, or a connector hanging down (on passenger side)<P>If you turn the ignition on, shut all the doors/hood/decklid, and open up the driver's door, and the ajar light does not come on, then you know it didnt get reconnected somewhere else when the alarm was installed.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||04-12-2001||07:59 PM||||Well my ajar light comes on when the doors are open and goes off when closed, the doors are off an 86GT and mine is an 84 SE.  But thanks, it was just curious though.||||reg||10
Z||000003||Wolfhound||04-12-2001||09:41 PM||||Inside the door, Is power windows, power lock and power mirror as far as electrical devices.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||1
